From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Artem Butusov <art.sormy@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 10:35:22 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] atbm6031: set the MAC through eth_hw_addr_set

Since 5.17 a netdev's address is const and shadowed: written by memcpy, it
leaves the shadow zero, and the first address-list change warns in
dev_addr_check, Incorrect netdev->dev_addr.
---
 hal_apollo/mac80211/iface.c | 6 ++----
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/hal_apollo/mac80211/iface.c b/hal_apollo/mac80211/iface.c
index 151a7fb..2ba9287 100644
--- a/hal_apollo/mac80211/iface.c
+++ b/hal_apollo/mac80211/iface.c
@@ -486,9 +486,7 @@ static int ieee80211_do_open(struct net_device *dev, bool coming_up)
 	 * this interface, if it has the special null one.
 	 */
 	if (is_zero_ether_addr(dev->dev_addr)) {
-		memcpy(dev->dev_addr,
-		       local->hw.wiphy->perm_addr,
-		       ETH_ALEN);
+		eth_hw_addr_set(dev, local->hw.wiphy->perm_addr);
 		memcpy(dev->perm_addr, dev->dev_addr, ETH_ALEN);
 
 		if (!is_valid_ether_addr(dev->dev_addr)) {
@@ -2530,7 +2528,7 @@ int ieee80211_if_add(struct ieee80211_local *local, const char *name,
 		goto fail;
 
 	ieee80211_assign_perm_addr(local, ndev, type);
-	memcpy(ndev->dev_addr, ndev->perm_addr, ETH_ALEN);
+	eth_hw_addr_set(ndev, ndev->perm_addr);
 	SET_NETDEV_DEV(ndev, wiphy_dev(local->hw.wiphy));
 
 	/* don't use IEEE80211_DEV_TO_SUB_IF because it checks too much */
-- 
